WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcribed from the narration in this video. Every figure the
speaker states matches the OECD time-use data behind this page.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
Hey, you wanna see how my day works?

2
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.520
Come, I'll walk you through it.

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.060
I start with 10 hours and
40 minutes of personal care.

4
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.860
Sleep, a bath, breakfast.

5
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.420
That's 25 minutes less than
the 35 country average.

6
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.660
We're efficient even at resting.

7
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.940
Then I'm at work.

8
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.440
6 hours and 8 minutes
of paid work a day.

9
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.980
The most in the data.

10
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.480
That's 96 minutes above
the 35 country average.

11
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.300
There's a word for it here.

12
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.440
Ikigai?

13
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.600
Finding purpose in what you do.

14
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.360
Lunch.

15
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.920
A quick bowl of ramen between shifts.

16
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.200
Then back to it.

17
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.360
At home, I spend about 2 hours
and 5 minutes on unpaid work.

18
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.960
The lowest of the 35 countries.

19
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.300
But here's something important.

20
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.300
Japanese women carry
a much bigger share.

21
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.940
About 161 minutes
more per day than men.

22
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.140
That's a conversation we're having.

23
00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.080
Leisure?

24
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.320
4 hours and 29 minutes.

25
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.300
That's 19 minutes below average.

26
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.380
But those moments feel earned.

27
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.780
And I'll work until about 71.

28
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:05.800
That's 5.6 years longer
than the average.

29
00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.800
Camille will have been
retired for a decade by then.

30
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.576
That's my day in Japan.
